      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town was officially founded in 1880 by George Adams, who platted it during a mining boom that drew prospectors to the San Luis Valley.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://townofcrestone.gov/pages/about-us",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1900, George Adams reopened a promising gold mine and built a railroad spur, sparking a brief early 20‑century boom.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crestone%2C_Colorado",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Baca Grant lands south of Crestone were subdivided in the 1970s into the Baca Grande development, creating thousands of new lots.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crestone%2C_Colorado",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Crestone has become a spiritual hub, hosting a Hindu temple, a Zen center, and several Tibetan Buddhist centers that attract seekers worldwide.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crestone%2C_Colorado",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Mule deer are a common sight in Crestone yards, reflecting the town’s long history as a deer park.",
